  "sourceDecisions": [
    "Historical Brann lordships and Airdmhor asylum remain despite war and partial occupation.",
    "Carnegie/Cerneige share stable family ID haus-cerneige; haus-carnegie remains an alias. Ten old Carnegie person IDs retain their identity while their house and outgoing links are reconciled.",
    "New origin evidence resolves Torcall Dubglais 1609 in Oglivy while retaining the old placeholder person ID. Etain Airdmhor receives 1672 and Faolan 1695 from the origin diagram.",
    "Existing origin-table years Cainneach 1561, Noracha 1590 and Vearga 1700 remain. Known death years, world IDs, portraits and partnership statuses remain intact.",
    "Cathmor 1650 / Taranach 1665 is documented source chronology. Taranachs two wives have separate child groups, consistent with Tuirens death in 1694.",
    "One Wemyss, three Dubglais, two Airdmhor and one Carnegie transmission gaps. Founders retain unknown years; dated early Airdmhor ancestors remain before the 16th-century gap.",
    "Dubhan is unchanged. Lagertha Grimr is shared across Wemyss and Dubglais, distinct from Lagertha Wellenkrone.",
    "No warrior illustrations or new portraits were supplied; canonical portraits are reused and absent images remain placeholders.",
    "Rory uses a single canonical card with four explicit partner/child lanes. Pair-midpoint alignment is disabled for those groups so it cannot undo the lane anchors; the authoring guard accepts this existing precise anchor and still rejects missing anchors."
  ],
